  "tools": [
   {
    "name": "update_step",
    "description": "Updates the checklist of the approved plan that the person watches above the prompt and in the Stepline pane. Call it with status \"completed\" as soon as a step is done, or \"skipped\" for a step the person drops. The first unfinished step counts as in progress, so use \"in_progress\" only when you start a step out of order. Steps are numbered as in the checklist Stepline gave you when the plan was approved."
   },
   {
    "name": "amend_plan",
    "description": "Changes the checklist of the approved plan that the person watches above the prompt and in the Stepline pane. \"add\" appends a step (title required) for work the person asks for that no step covers. \"retitle\" renames step N (step and title) when the person changes what a step means. \"aside\" shows a few words under the current step while you do unplanned work such as a fix or a tangent (title; an empty title clears it, and so does your next update_step call). Don’t add steps for your own sub-tasks."
   }
